#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""M3Z5 (DIAGNOSTIC ONLY): register a crypto_functions table so g_crypto_funcs != NULL.

M3Z3/M3Z4 readouts: two consumers in a row fault on the NULL corecrypto table
(+0x28 ccsha1_di in generatePlatformUUID; +0x150 random_kmem_ctx_size_fn via
crypto_random_kmem_ctx_size <- kmem_crypto_init). Nothing in the M3 kernel calls
register_crypto_functions (its caller is the corecrypto kext). Layout per
xnu-8796.101.5 libkern/libkern/crypto/register_crypto.h (56 u64 slots, 0x1C0 B;
+0x28 sha1_di / +0x38 sha384_di / +0x40 sha512_di match the disassembly).

M3Z7: reg also installs cckprng funcs (prng @0x...7164460: initialized=1,
  funcs 0x468..0x490 = no-op except generate(ctx,cpu,n,out) -> xorshift; ctx
  0x...7B082B0 = &table) -- read_random had blr'd NULL refresh (LR 0x...73B63A8).
Code (crypto_reg.S, 0x2D0 B + 0x1C0 B table at VA 0x...73E0500, NOP hole):
  reg    hooked at initialize_screen's ret (0x...73B087C, reached before P9):
         register_crypto_functions(&table), then ret.
  slots 0x140 random_generate  -> xorshift64 seeded from cntpct (NOT secure)
        0x148 random_uniform   -> cntpct % bound
        0x150 random_kmem_ctx_size -> 256
        0x158 random_kmem_init -> 0
  every other slot -> its own trap: writes an M3E crumb with CODE = slot offset,
        ESR = 0xC0DE0000|slot, ELR = caller x30, FAR = x0, then b to the M3E tail
        (halt_tail makes it `b .`) -> monitor v3.7 row 5 names the next missing slot.
Usage: crypto_reg.py IN OUT  (M3U -> fix_console_pa -> halt_tail -> uuid_skip -> this).
Not combinable with canary.py / patch_trace --set console / panic_rec (same site/hole).
"""
